/ |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[Consumer Reports]] |date=26 November 2018}}</ref><ref name=:13>{{cite journal | last1 = Suez | first1 = J | last2 = Zmora | first2 = N | last3 = Zilbrerman-Schapira | first3 = G | last4 = Mor | first4 = U | last5 = Dori-Bachash | first5 = M | last6 = Bashiardes | first6 = S | last7 = Zur | first7 = M | last8 = Regev-LehavI | first8 = D | last9 = Ben-Zeev Brik | first9 = R | last10 = Federici | first10 = S | last11 = Horn | first11 = M | last12 = Cohen | first12 = Y | last13 = Moor | first13 = AE | last14 = Zeevy | first14 = D | last15 = Korem | first15 = T | last16 = Harmelin | first16 = A | last17 = Itzkovitz | first17 = S | last18 = Maharshak | first18 = N | last19 = Shibolet | first19 = O | last20 = Pevnser-Fishcher | first20 = M | last21 = Shapiro | first21 = H | last22 = Sharon | first22 = I | last23 = Halpern | first23 = Z | last24 = Segal | first24 = E | last25 = Elinav | first25 = E | year = 2018 | title = Post-antibiotic gut mucosal microbiome reconstitution is impaired by probiotics and improved by autologous FMT | url = | journal = Cell | volume = 174 | issue = 6| pages = 1406–1423 | pmid = 30193113 | doi = 10.1016/j.cell.2018.08.047 }}</ref> vaginal microbiome transplantation<ref>{{cite news |last1=Davis |first1=Nicola |title=Vaginal fluid transplants could cure bacterial vaginosis |url=https://www.theguardian.com/society/2019/oct/07/vaginal-fluid-transplants-could-cure-bacterial-vaginosis |accessdate=19 November 2020 |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=7 October 2019}}</ref><ref name=:15>{{cite journal | last1 = Lev-Sagie | first1 = A | last2 = Goldman-Wohl | first2 = D | last3 = Cohen | first3 = Y | last4 = Dori-Bachash | first4 = M | last5 = Leshem | first5 = A | last6 = Mor | first6 = U | last7 = Strahilevitz | first7 = J | last8 = Moses | first8 = A | last9 = Shapiro | first9 = H | last10 = Yagel | first10 = S | last11 = Elinav | first11 = E | year = 2019 | title = Vaginal Microbiome Transplantation in women with