=== Personalized Nutrition ===
In 2014 Elinav discovered that people consuming identical foods and additives, such as non-nutritive sweeteners,<ref name=":0" /><ref name="NNS">Jotham Suez, Yotam Cohen, Rafael Valdés-Mas, Uria Mor, Mally Dori-Bachash, Sara Federici, Niv Zmora, Avner Leshem, Melina Heinemann, Raquel Linevsky, Maya Zur, Rotem Ben-Zeev Brik, Aurelie Bukimer, Shimrit Eliyahu-Miller, Alona Metz, Ruthy Fischbein, Olga Sharov, Sergey Malitsky, Maxim Itkin, Noa Stettner, Alon Harmelin, Hagit Shapiro, Christoph K. Stein-Thoeringer, Eran Segal, Eran Elinav | Personalized microbiome-driven effects of non-nutritive sweeteners on human glucose tolerance, {{cite journal |title=Prof. Eran Elinav |journal=Cell|year=2022 |doi=10.1016/j.cell.2022.07.016 |pmid=35987213 |s2cid=251667371 |last1=Suez |first1=J. |last2=Cohen |first2=Y. |last3=Valdés-Mas |first3=R. |last4=Mor |first4=U. |last5=Dori-Bachash |first5=M. |last6=Federici |first6=S. |last7=Zmora |first7=N. |last8=Leshem |first8=A. |last9=Heinemann |first9=M. |last10=Linevsky |first10=R. |last11=Zur |first11=M. |last12=Ben-Zeev Brik |first12=R. |last13=Bukimer |first13=A. |last14=Eliyahu-Miller |first14=S. |last15=Metz |first15=A. |last16=Fischbein |first16=R. |last17=Sharov |first17=O. |last18=Malitsky |first18=S. |last19=Itkin |first19=M. |last20=Stettner |first20=N. |last21=Harmelin |first21=A. |last22=Shapiro |first22=H. |last23=Stein-Thoeringer |first23=C. K. |last24=Segal |first24=E. |last25=Elinav |first25=E. |volume=185 |issue=18 |pages=3307–3328.e19 |doi-access= }}</ref> general foods<ref name=":1">{{cite journal | last1 = Ze'Evy | first1 = D | last2 = Korem | first2 = T | last3 = Rothschild | first3 = D | last4 = Weinberger | first4 = A | last5 = Zmora | first5 = N | last6 = Israeli | first6 = D | last7 = Ben-Yacov | first7 = O | last8 = Lador | first8 = D | last9 = Avnit-Sagi | first9 = T | last10 = Lotan-Pompan | first10 = M | last11 = Suez | first11 = J | last12 = Ali Mahdi | first12 = J | last13 = Matot | first13 = E | last14 = Malka | first14 = G | last15 = Kosower | first15 = N | last16 = Rein | first16 = M | last17 = Zilberman-Schapira | first17 = G | last18 = Dohnalova | first18 = L | last19 = Pevsner-Fischer | first19 = M | last20 = Bikovsky | first20 = R | last21 = Halpern | first21 = Z | last22 = Elinav | first22 = E | last23 = Segal | first23 = E | year = 2015| title = Personalized Nutrition for the Prediction of Glycemic Responses | url = https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0092867415014816 | journal = Cell | volume = 163 | issue = 5| pages = 1079–1094 | pmid = 26590418 | doi = 10.1016/j.cell.2015.11.001 }}</ref> and bread,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Yong |first1=Ed |title=Scientists Pit Sourdough Against White Bread—With Surprising Results |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/science/archive/2017/06/sourdough-versus-white-bread/529260/ |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[The Atlantic]] |date=6 June 2017}}</ref><ref name=:11>{{cite journal | last1 = Korem | first1 = T | last2 = Zeevi | first2 = D | last3 = Zmora | first3 = N | last4 = Weissbrod | first4 = O | last5 = Bar | first5 = N | last6 = Lotan-Pompan | first6 = M | last7 = Avnit-Sagi | first7 = T | last8 = Kosower | first8 = N | last9 = Malka | first9 = G | last10 = Rein | first10 = M | last11 = Suez | first11 = J | last12 = Goldberg | first12 = B | last13 = Weinberger | first13 = A | last14 = Levy | first14 = AA | last15 = Elinav | first15 = E | last16 = Segal | first16 = E | year = 2017 | title = Bread affects clinical parameters and induces gut microbiome associated personal glycemic responses | url = | journal = Cell Metabolism | volume = 25 | issue = 6| pages = 1243–1253 | pmid = 28591632 | doi = 10.1016/j.cmet.2017.05.002 }}</ref> feature a unique and personalized glycemic response, thereby potentially explaining the lack of uniform metabolic responses to generalized dietary approaches.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Medaris Miller |first1=Anna |title=Should You Take a Genetic Test to Find the Best Diet for You? |url=https://health.usnews.com/wellness/articles/2018-01-16/should-you-take-a-genetic-test-to-find-the-best-diet-for-you |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[U.S. News & World Report]] |date=16 January 2018}}</ref> Personalized dietary recommendations,<ref>{{cite news |title=Why do some people put on weight and not others – and can we change it? |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/2lw8qKp7NFf7N7mhbXmsY34/why-do-some-people-put-on-weight-and-not-others-and-can-we-change-it |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[BBC]]}}</ref> based on individualized dietary,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Doherty |first1=Jimmy |title=Food Unwrapped Diet Special |url=https://www.channel4.com/programmes/food-unwrapped/on-demand/59510-014 |website=channel4 |accessdate=19 November 2020}}</ref> clinical and microbiota data, improved pre-diabetes control.<ref name=":1" /> He similarly showed, that consumption of probiotics<ref name=:12>{{cite journal | last1 = Zmora | first1 = N | last2 = Zilbrerman-Schapira | first2 = G | last3 = Suez | first3 = J | last4 = Mor | first4 = U | last5 = Dori-Bachash | first5 = M | last6 = Bashiardes | first6 = S | last7 = Kotler | first7 = E | last8 = Zur | first8 = M | last9 = Regev-LehavI | first9 = D | last10 = Ben-Zeev Brik | first10 = R | last11 = Federici | first11 = S | last12 = Cohen | first12 = Y | last13 = Linevsky | first13 = R | last14 = Rothschild | first14 = D | last15 = Moor | first15 = AE | last16 = Ben-Moshe | first16 = S | last17 = Harmelin | first17 = A | last18 = Itzkovitz | first18 = S | last19 = Maharshak | first19 = N | last20 = Shibolet | first20 = O | last21 = Shapiro | first21 = H | last22 = Pevnser-Fishcher | first22 = M | last23 = Sharon | first23 = I | last24 = Halpern | first24 = Z | last25 = Segal | first25 = E | last26 = Elinav | first26 = E | year = 2018 | title = Personalized gut mucosal colonization resistance to empiric probiotics is associated with unique host and microbiome features | url = https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0092867418311024 | journal = Cell | volume = 174 | issue = 6| pages = 1388–1405 | pmid = 30193112 | doi = 10.1016/j.cell.2018.08.041 | bibcode = 2018Cell..174.1388Z }}</ref> leads to a person-specific colonization resistance and physiological patterns.<ref>{{cite news |title=Is whole wheat bread healthier? It depends on the person, study suggests |url=https://www.ctvnews.ca/health/article/is-whole-wheat-bread-healthier-it-depends-on-the-person-study-suggests/ |access-date=19 November 2020 |publisher=CTVNews.ca |date=6 June 2017}}</ref>

=== Nutritional timing and the Microbiota ===
Elinav discovered, that the [[gut microbiota]]  features a compositional and functional diurnal activity during a 24-hour cycle, which is dictated by host and environmental factors, mainly by the timing in food consumption.<ref>{{cite news |last1=David |first1=Lawrence |title=Tracking the Daily Rhythms of the Microbiome |url=https://www.sciencefriday.com/segments/tracking-the-daily-rhythms-of-the-microbiome/ |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=Science Friday |date=12 February 2016}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{cite journal | last1 = Thaiss | first1 = CA | last2 = Ze'Evi | first2 = D | last3 = Levy | first3 = M | last4 = Zilberman-Schapira | first4 = G | last5 = Suez | first5 = J | last6 = Tengeler | first6 = AC | last7 = Abramson | first7 = L | last8 = Katz | first8 = MN | last9 = Korem | first9 = T | last10 = Zmora | first10 = N | last11 = Kuperman | first11 = Y | last12 = Biton | first12 = Y | last13 = Gilad | first13 = S | last14 = Harmelin | first14 = A | last15 = Shapiro | first15 = H | last16 = Halpern | first16 = Z | last17 = Segal | first17 = E | last18 = Elinav | first18 = E | year = 2014 | title = Trans-kingdom control of microbiota diurnal oscillations promotes metabolic homeostasis | url = https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0092867414012367 | journal = Cell | volume = 159 | issue = 3| pages = 514–29 | pmid = 25417104 | doi = 10.1016/j.cell.2014.09.048 }}</ref> These microbiota diurnal activities are tightly coordinated with the host gastrointestinal and systemic circadian activity,<ref name=":4">{{cite journal | last1 = Thaiss | first1 = CA | last2 = Levy | first2 = M | last3 = Korem | first3 = T | last4 = Zweevi | first4 = D | last5 = Jaitin | first5 = DA | last6 = David | first6 = E | last7 = Dohnalova | first7 = L | last8 = Meijer | first8 = M | last9 = Kartvelishvily | first9 = E | last10 = Pevsner-Fischer | first10 = M | last11 = Gatt | first11 = ME | last12 = Harmelin | first12 = A | last13 = Halpern | first13 = Z | last14 = Amit | first14 = I | last15 = Segal | first15 = E | last16 = Elinav | first16 = E | year = 2016 | title = Microbiota diurnal rhythmicity program host trascriptome oscillations | url = | journal = Cell | volume = 167 | issue = 5| pages = 1495–1510 | pmid = 27912092 | doi = 10.1016/j.molcel.2016.11.027 }}</ref> while disruption of circadian activity by jet-lag<ref>{{cite news |last1=Oaklander |first1=Mandy |title=How Jet Lag Can Contribute to Obesity |url=https://time.com/3513135/how-jet-lag-can-contribute-to-obesity/ |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[Time (magazine)|Time]] |date=16 October 2014}}</ref> or shift work may lead to alterations in the microbiota behavior, which contribute to the development of common metabolic,<ref name=":2" /> immune<ref name="TimurT">Tuganbaev T, Mor U, Bashiardes S, Liwinski T, Nobs SP, Leshem A, Dori-Bachash M, Pinker EY, Ratiner K, Adlung LK, Federici S, Kleimeyer C, Moresi C, Yamada T, Cohen Y, Massalha H, Massasa E, Kuperman Y, Koni PA, Harmelin A, Gao N, Itzkovitz S, Honda, Shapiro H, Elinav E. 2020. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0092867420310692 Diet diurnally regulates SI microbiome-epithelial-immune homeostasis and enteritis]. ''Cell'', Epub. PMID 32888430</ref> and liver diseases.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Greenberg |first1=Larry M. |title=How Disrupting Your Gut's Rhythm Affects Your Health |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-disrupting-your-guts-rhythm-affects-your-health-1488164400 |accessdate=19 November 2020 |publisher=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |date=27 February 2017}}</ref><ref name=":4" />

==Awards and recognition==
Elinav was awarded the Rappaport prize for biomedical research in 2015,<ref name="Rappaport">{{cite web |title=Prof. Eran Elinav – Prize for Senior Israeli Bio-Medical Researcher |url=https://www.rappaport-prize.org.il/en/eran-elinav |website=Rappaport Prize Awards |accessdate=17 July 2020}}</ref> the Levinson award for basic science research in 2016,<ref>[https://www.weizmann.ac.il/acadaff/awards-and-honors/scientific-council-prizes/prizelist-year?field_year_value=2016 Awards And Honors | Scientific Council Prizes- 2016], Weizmann Institute of Science</ref> the Landau prize of Immunology in 2018<ref>{{cite web |title=Eran Elinav |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200812215356/https://culture.pais.co.il/Landau/Pages/eran_elinav.aspx |archive-date= 12 August 2020 |url=https://culture.pais.co.il/Landau/Pages/eran_elinav.aspx |website=Pais – Arts and Sciences Awards |accessdate=17 July 2020}}</ref> and [[The EFSD and the Novo Nordisk Foundation Precision Diabetes Medicine Award]] in 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |title=EFSD-NNF Precision Diabetes Medicine Award Programme |url=https://www.europeandiabetesfoundation.org/efsd-nnf-precision-diabetes-medicine-award-programme.html |access-date=2024-12-31 |website=www.europeandiabetesfoundation.org}}</ref> Elinav was inducted into the [[European Molecular Biology Organization ]] (EMBO) in 2017,<ref>{{cite web |title=Eran Elinav EMBO |url=https://people.embo.org/profile/eran-elinav |website=European Molecular Biology Organization  |accessdate=3 June 2026}}</ref> the American Academy of Microbiology in 2021,<ref>{{cite web |title=Eran Elinav |url=https://www.weizmann.ac.il/immunology/congratulations-prof-eran-elinav-0 |website=Weizmann Institute of Science |accessdate=17 November 2022}}</ref> the [[German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina]]<ref>{{Cite web |title=Prof. Dr. Eran Elinav |url=https://www.leopoldina.org/mitgliederverzeichnis/mitglieder/member/Member/show/eran-elinav/ |access-date=13 May 2025 |publisher=German National Academy of Sciences Leopoldina |language=German}}</ref> and The European Academy for Cancer Sciences in 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |title=New EACS Fellows 2025 |url=https://www.europeancanceracademy.eu/news/new-eacs-fellows-2025|access-date=8 December 2025 |publisher=The European Academy for Cancer Sciences |language=English}}</ref>

